4d595de742e2442af3512d432eda7dbef9126d885bc0570cf7"},"seconds":9.61172890663147,"seed":277141143378517636,"stop":"eos","text":"Let's define the variables and set up the equations based on the information given.\n\nLet \\( x \\) be the number of questions Frank answered correctly.\nLet \\( y \\) be the number of questions Frank answered incorrectly.\nSince Frank answered 80 questions, we have:\n\\[ x + y = 80. \\]\n\nEach correct answer scores 5 points, and each incorrect answer scores -2 points. Frank's total score is 232 points, so we can write the equation:\n\\[ 5x - 2y = 232. \\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n1. \\( x + y = 80 \\)\n2. \\( 5x - 2y = 232 \\)\n\nWe can solve this system step by step. First, solve the first equation for \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = 80 - x. \\]\n\nNext, substitute \\( y = 80 - x \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 5x - 2(80 - x) = 232. \\]\n\\[ 5x - 160 + 2x = 232. \\]\n\\[ 7x - 160 = 232. \\]\n\\[ 7x = 392. \\]\n\\[ x = 56. \\]\n\nSo, Frank answered \\( x = 56 \\) questions correctly. To verify, we can find \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = 80 - 56 = 24. \\]\n\nNow, check the score:\n\\[ 5(56) - 2(24) = 280 - 48 = 232. \\]\nThe score is correct. Therefore, the number of questions Frank answered correctly is \\(\\boxed{56}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{56}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:534"}
